## When CI fails but local check passed

The Actions job page may not expose full logs to agents. **Fetch with `gh`**, not the web UI alone.

1. Re-run scoped local check first (match failing matrix cell: `group=harness`, web job, etc.).
2. Extract **run ID** from `/actions/runs/<RUN_ID>/...`.
3. Pull failed-step output:

```bash
gh run view <RUN_ID> --repo AlexsanderHamir/Hamix --json conclusion,status,displayTitle,headSha,jobs
gh run view <RUN_ID> --repo AlexsanderHamir/Hamix --log-failed
```

PowerShell (tail large logs):

```powershell
gh run view <RUN_ID> --repo AlexsanderHamir/Hamix --log-failed 2>&1 | Select-Object -Last 120
```

4. Report: which job/matrix cell failed, package/test names, last error lines — not just exit code 1.

### Do not

- Claim CI is opaque without trying `gh run view --log-failed`.
- Use `gh run watch` as the fix loop (use local check instead).

